      "content": "It sounds like you are catastrophizing a specific failure into an existential crisis, which is a very painful but treatable type of thinking that needs to be addressed. Realize that your parents love you for who you truly are, not for the label of success you thought they expected from you. Please consider reaching out to a therapist who is skilled in cognitive behavioral therapy to help dismantle these all-or-nothing thoughts and support you in reclaiming your self-worth.",
      "source": "target",
